   "notes": "16 King's Parade (Troon). Mock-Tudor black-and-white timber front (black studs/posts with carved bracket heads, white render panels), upper floors jettied. 1st floor: projecting multi-light bay windows (sash lights with side returns) - one clearly seen at the south end, a second at the north end; 2nd floor: paired multi-pane windows above them. Black shopfront with 'TROON' lettering and a cream retractable awning; a brown timber side door/panel at the north end next to Caffe Nero. Exact bay split and roof/dormers not seen clearly; window count 2 per floor is a best reading of oblique photos."
